 We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $(,)$ to indicate that the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ to indicate that the endpoints *are* included.\n\nOur interval contains only brackets. So, the endpoints *are* included. \n\n$$\nx\\in [-11,3]\n$$\n\nTherefore, our interval can be expressed as the following inequality:\n\n$$\n-11\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,x\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,3\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502715 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fd70390-8caf-561a-910f-14961cb9f4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502637} {:answer/id #uuid "431352d0-7c7a-58b5-915f-029502f88355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-4,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502647} {:answer/id #uuid "68eb80a8-2b59-50f6-b0fb-8cebd06fff56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502668} {:answer/id #uuid "9996ae63-c4c4-5c69-82bf-10db9836b526" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502692} {:answer/id #uuid "db77b9a5-a903-5773-99bc-3a69da2affc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "431352d0-7c7a-58b5-915f-029502f88355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-4,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502647} :answer-field/id #uuid "60d400d7-cc0a-53e9-8c5c-d69c00c39617" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e71ef6b0-33d5-574b-a412-76bd2763d136" :question/problem "The inequality $-4\\le x\\le -2$ can be expressed in interval notation as" :question/worked-solution "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nOur inequality contains only \"or equal to\" symbols. So, the endpoints $-4$ and $-2$ *are* included. \n\n$$\n-4\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,x\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\n[-4,-2]\n$$\n\nMore formally, we can also write\n\n$$\nx\\in [-4,-2].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502718 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1626e470-cad1-5f9d-9ec9-727a32fd1da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11 \\le x < 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502636} {:answer/id #uuid "4342b6ad-f0f0-5ac9-b979-b2c99f19fac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11 < x < 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502648} {:answer/id #uuid "4de629f1-5eba-57cc-9794-28eaabc6d1cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x < - 11$ or $x > 8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502658} {:answer/id #uuid "779e535b-e467-53d6-a379-d26f9d0eccc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11 < x \\le 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502677} {:answer/id #uuid "935f93d8-33c3-5010-ae21-4b4e7a1df253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11 \\le x \\le 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "935f93d8-33c3-5010-ae21-4b4e7a1df253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11 \\le x \\le 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502687} :answer-field/id #uuid "99bbbcdd-7ca0-5ed9-8647-ac2286849187" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb411cd3-b0bc-5d55-b10a-a980eed0b2af" :question/problem "Which inequality corresponds to the interval $x ∈ [- 11, 8]$?" :question/worked-solution "Every interval can be expressed as an inequality. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses ${\\color{red}{(}}\\phantom{0} \\phantom{0}{\\color{red}{)}}$ to indicate that the endpoints are *not* included.\n- Brackets ${\\color{blue}{[}}\\phantom{0} \\phantom{0}{\\color{blue}{]}}$ to indicate that the endpoints *are* included.\n\nOur interval contains only brackets. So, the endpoints are *included*.\n\n$$\nx\\in {\\color{blue}{[}}-11, 8{\\color{blue}{]}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our interval can be expressed as the following inequality:\n\n$$\n-11 \\,\\,{\\color{blue}{\\le}}\\,\\, x \\,\\,{\\color{blue}{\\le}}\\,\\, 8\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Converting Between Intervals and Inequalities: Closed Intervals"}]}
